 Add `--json` to get a JSON object instead.
 
+### Caching
+
+Parsing dominates the runtime on large files. Pass `--cache` to store the
+parsed records on disk and reuse them on the next run over the same file:
+
+```
+logslice --cache huge.log --count-by level   # parses and caches
+logslice --cache huge.log --level error      # served from the cache
+```
+
+Cached results are stored as JSON, one entry per log file. The cache key
+includes the file's resolved path, size and modification time, so editing or
+appending to a log invalidates its entry.
+
+The cache directory is resolved in this order: `$LOGSLICE_CACHE_DIR` (used
+as-is) if set, otherwise `$XDG_CACHE_HOME/logslice`, otherwise
+`~/.cache/logslice`.
+
+Entries expire after a configurable time-to-live. `--cache-ttl SECONDS`
+(default `3600`) controls how long a cached entry is considered fresh; once it
+is older than that, the file is re-parsed and the entry rewritten. Delete the
+cache directory to clear it immediately.
+
 ## Development
 
 ```
